{title: 432 - Shall We Gather at the River}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #432 • HANSON PLACE • 8.7.8.7.}
{lyricist: Robert Lowry}
{composer: Robert Lowry}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 432}
{meta: tune HANSON PLACE}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.7.}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]Shall we gather at the river,
[Ab7]Where bright angel feet have trod,
[Db]With its crystal tide forever
[Ab]Flowing by [Ab7]the throne of [Db]God?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Gb]Yes, we'll gather at the [Db]river,
[Ab7]the beautiful, the beautiful [Db]river;
[Gb]gather with the saints at the [Db]river
[Ab]that flows by [Ab7]the throne of [Db]God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]On the margin of the river,
[Ab7]washing up its silver spray,
[Db]we will walk and worship ever,
[Ab]all the happy [Ab7]golden [Db]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]Ere we reach the shining river,
[Ab7]lay we every burden down;
[Db]grace our spirits will deliver,
[Ab]and provide [Ab7]a robe and [Db]crown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]Soon we'll reach the shining river,
[Ab7]soon our pilgrimage will cease;
[Db]soon our happy hearts will quiver
[Ab]with the melody [Ab7]of [Db]peace.
{end_of_verse}
